#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# longest

#% text
# `longest(p)` makes the runs and repetitions inside the pattern `p` take as much as possible first; String patterns are greedy by default; `longest` makes it explicit.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
string_cases("abcdefg", string_expression(x__, longest(__)) :> x)
#% output
#= ["abcdef"]

#% cell
string_cases("0111011110", longest(repeated("1")))
#% output
#= ["111", "1111"]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# In a term pattern a sequence variable takes the shortest run first; `longest(xs__)` makes it take the longest, before the unmarked runs; `longest(p, k)` gives it priority `k` among the marked runs (higher first).

#% cell
rewrite([a, b, c, d], [x__, longest(y__)] :> [x, y])
#% output
#= [[a], [b, c, d]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `shortest`, `string_expression`, `string_cases`
